// random.zm -- a minimal native module: one function, reading real
// entropy from the OS, since Ziman has no other source of
// non-determinism to build a PRNG on top of (no clock/time builtin
// either, so there's nothing to seed one from even if we wanted a
// Ziman-side PRNG instead). Deliberately not a general PRNG API --
// see docs/DESIGN.md's "random" entry.

pub native fn random_bytes(n: int) -> [byte]
